    {
      "block_id": "h2-11",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Primary Risk: Validate Test Overlap",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "**`test_validate.py` (1,797 lines, 127 tests)** and **`test_validate_git_state.py` (390 lines, 27 tests)** contain:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- **1 exact duplicate** (test_collect_git_state_non_repo) - **~15 near-duplicates** across dirty policy, git state model, porcelain parsing, and worktree readiness - **Same Stage 5 git-state tests** were added to test_validate.py first, then test_validate_git_state.py was created as a cleaner dedicated file — but the originals were never removed - **`test_validate.py` does NOT need to keep any git-state tests** — they were added as part of Stage 5 and are fully covered in `test_validate_git_state.py`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "**Recommended:** remove 19 tests from test_validate.py (all git-state tests starting at line 1469), reducing it by ~310 lines. No coverage loss.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-15",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Brittle/Low-Value Test Patterns",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1. **Private helper assertion tests** — `test_validate.py` has many tests that import and assert against private functions (`_parse_git_status_branch`, `_parse_git_status_porcelain_line`, `_check_dirty_policy`, etc.). These are implementation-detail tests. While they provide fast feedback during development, they are brittle to refactoring and should be supplemented (not replaced) by public-behavior tests that exercise these helpers through `tool.run()`.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "2. **`# type: ignore[call-arg]` on line 1773** of `test_validate.py` — Violates AGENTS.md rule against inline `# type: ignore`. Pre-existing from Stage 4.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-18",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "3. **Exact string matching on refusal messages** — Several receipt emission tests match exact strings like `\"Command timed out after 30s\"`. Brittle if wording changes.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "4. **Test files with 0 test functions** — `tests/governance/test_local_action_envelope.py` (434 lines) contains no `test_` functions. May be a conftest or fixture file with misleading name.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
